---
const features = [
  { title: "Choose the right boundaries", text: "Capture or import a photo. Review the physical card edge and the meaningful printed boundary. Suggested pins are a starting point; adjust them where needed." },
  { title: "Check front and back", text: "Inspect left/right and top/bottom centering on each side. A centered front alone does not tell you the back's centering or the card's full condition." },
  { title: "Keep a useful record", text: "Use zoom and manual controls to review your photo. Save or share the marked result with context about the boundaries and the side you checked." },
];
---
<section id="features" class="py-16 md:py-24 border-t border-white/5">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-[32px] font-bold mb-10">A centering check you can inspect</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {features.map((feature, index) => (
        <article class="rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-white/5 p-7">
          <span class="text-brand-teal font-mono text-sm">0{index + 1}</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-4 mb-3">{feature.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">{feature.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">Blur, glare, sleeves, tilt and ambiguous card layouts can make a boundary hard to identify. More zoom does not add image detail. Retake the photo or leave the measurement unresolved when the edge is unclear.</p>
  </div>
</section>
